---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript';
const title = "Klaviyo vs Postscript for Shopify: 2026 comparison";
const desc = "Decide who owns SMS, and verify Postscript email access before planning a full platform replacement.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Postscript replace Klaviyo email?",
    "answer": "Postscript advertises phased email rollout. Verify account access and journey parity before planning replacement."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does an integration prevent duplicate cart messages?",
    "answer": "Not by itself. Assign trigger ownership and test exclusions, queued messages and event delays."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which SMS tool converts better?",
    "answer": "This page has no comparative delivery or conversion experiment. Evaluate your program without assuming a universal winner."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Klaviyo vs Postscript for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Decide who owns SMS, and verify Postscript email access before planning a full platform replacement.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Start with the channels you are replacing</h2>
        <p>An email migration and an SMS ownership decision require different evidence. List the channels you operate today and which journeys must survive. Do not remove an email sender because a vendor is described as SMS-first, or assume every advertised channel is already available to your account.</p>
        <h2>The old SMS-only comparison is incomplete</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/postscript-sms-marketing">Postscript listing</a> now advertises SMS, RCS and email, and explicitly says email is rolling out in phases. It also lists two-way messaging and Shopify data use. The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/klaviyo-email-marketing">Klaviyo listing</a> advertises email and SMS alongside automated workflows. Checked November 24, 2026: these descriptions establish advertised scope, not universal account access or a conversion advantage.</p>
        <h2>Proposed drop-day exercise: a reply before purchase</h2>
        <p>This exercise has not been performed. Prepare a test-only product drop message and have an eligible test subscriber reply with a sizing question. Check where the reply appears, who receives an alert, what an automated response can say, and how a human takes over. Place a test order before the follow-up is due and inspect whether that follow-up stops. Record actual ownership and logs rather than assigning invented scores.</p>
        <h2>Write the split-stack contract</h2>
        <p>If Klaviyo retains email and Postscript handles SMS, name the sender for welcome, cart, sale and winback messages. Record the customer identifiers used across systems, order event source, channel-specific permission, opt-out timestamp and any delay in propagation. A purchase exclusion and an SMS opt-out solve different problems; neither should be treated as a substitute for the other.</p>
        <h2>Rehearse delayed events and opt-outs</h2>
        <p>In an isolated setup, test a purchase arriving after a message was queued, an unsubscribe while a flow is waiting, and a reply that needs staff attention. Inspect behavior in both systems and decide which automation must pause if data stops arriving. Do not assume listing an integration means every exclusion or frequency cap is shared automatically.</p>
        <h2>Define message budgets before comparing bills</h2>
        <p>Provide each vendor with destination countries, expected recipients, campaign frequency and the actual draft text. Ask how long messages, Unicode, media, carrier fees, included credits, minimums and overages affect the quote. Add retained email costs and integration maintenance when pricing a split stack. A subscriber count alone does not specify an SMS bill.</p>
        <h2>Assess safeguards without claiming legal clearance</h2>
        <p>Ask the account owner to demonstrate permission records, opt-out processing, destination eligibility and sending schedules for the intended program. Document who approves audiences and who handles replies. Supplier guardrails are useful features, but this comparison does not establish that a particular campaign or imported list satisfies applicable requirements.</p>
        <h2>If Postscript email is offered to your account</h2>
        <p>Request access and plan scope in writing. Rebuild the email welcome and cart journeys in draft, including product content, exclusions, authentication, reporting and suppression export. Inspect parity before retiring the current email service. If access is unavailable, compare Postscript as the SMS layer and retain a separate email owner; do not extrapolate from a phased rollout announcement.</p>
        <h2>Decision and measurement</h2>
        <p>Keep channels together when the demonstrated workflow, staffing and quote support it. Split them when the SMS operation has a concrete requirement the alternative demonstrably resolves and someone can maintain the handoff. Compare completed orders and contribution after message and operating costs; avoid adding email-attributed and SMS-attributed sales as if they were disjoint incremental revenue.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-postscript">Omnisend vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/recart-vs-postscript">Recart vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">Email apps for fashion stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Klaviyo vs Postscript for Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
